{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: model forecasts are systematically too high versus realized prices, especially beyond ~day 10. Apply a downward level shift (larger for longer horizons).",
    "Trend underreaction / lag in downtrends: when recent history is falling, the model continues to project a flatter/higher path and misses the speed of decline. Increase sensitivity to recent negative momentum (steepen projected declines).",
    "Horizon-dependent error growth: forecast error increases with lead time; near-term (days 1–5) is closer, while days 15–30 show the largest overestimation. Use a horizon-based correction that ramps down forecasts with time.",
    "Insufficient mean-reversion to lower regime: after a regime break lower, the model reverts upward too aggressively (projects rebounds that don’t materialize). Damp upward mean-reversion terms when the last 30d trend is negative.",
    "Overshoot on minor rebounds: during small realized bounces, the model extrapolates into larger/longer rebounds (mid-horizon hump) that are not observed. Cap rebound amplitude and duration unless confirmed by multi-day positive momentum."
  ]
}
